  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-ef1234567890",
    "name": "Sayly API",
    "description": "Sayly language-exchange backend for frontend code review.\n\n## Setup\n1. Import this collection and `Sayly-Local.postman_environment.json`.\n2. Select the **Sayly Local** environment.\n3. Start the API (`cd backend/server && npm run dev`). Default base URL: `http://localhost:4000`.\n4. Optional: seed demo users with `npx tsx scripts/seed-demo-users.ts`.\n\n## Demo accounts (password: `sayly123`)\n- `maria@sayly.test`\n- `james@sayly.test`\n- `lucia@sayly.test`\n- `sayly@demo.com`\n\n## Auth\nCollection auth is Bearer `{{accessToken}}`.\nLogin / Register / Refresh test scripts save `accessToken`, `refreshToken`, and `userId` into the active environment.\n\n## Suggested review flow\nAuth → Languages → Onboarding/Profile → Discover → Connections → Chat → Media → Safety.\n\n## Notes\n- `/discover` and `/discovery` are aliases.\n- `/messaging/*` routes are legacy aliases of `/conversations/*`.\n- `/matching/*` returns 501 (stubs).\n- Socket.IO events are not covered here; use the HTTP chat fallbacks for review.\n- Swagger UI (if enabled): `{{baseUrl}}/api-docs`",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
